WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.950
To close, where this fits.

2
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:06.770
The workbook's DNS, DHCP and IPAM
book makes the vendor-neutral case,

3
00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.307
from split-brain to the policy plane,

4
00:00:09.307 --> 00:00:14.212
and the research deep dive on Infoblox
DDI covers the platform itself.

5
00:00:14.212 --> 00:00:19.274
The decisions to take are which option
for each cloud and impact level, one named

6
00:00:19.274 --> 00:00:21.958
owner for every zone,
where DNSSEC keys live,

7
00:00:21.958 --> 00:00:24.488
and how address blocks reach each cloud.

8
00:00:24.488 --> 00:00:27.894
The next steps start with
Infoblox: ask for the Government

9
00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:31.513
Cloud boundary and a feature
matrix for government accounts.

10
00:00:31.513 --> 00:00:35.883
Then confirm Azure Government
availability, size NIOS-X capacity if

11
00:00:35.883 --> 00:00:40.100
you want cloud forwarders, and test
forwarding in both directions.

12
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.025
This is research under review, not an
endorsement by any federal agency.

13
00:00:45.025 --> 00:00:45.840
Thank you.
